3427fad6209be3dc80365bdd5cd83455e62d17440b554ceb37f4d737f6cff43","file":"preprints/Translative-covering-densities-of-order-n-log-n-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":49,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"27ad0c6ab21a74940f8d4fc267fc2687525c9de00f9ea15ede893b5b1c5c31b3","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Translative-covering-densities-of-order-n-log-n-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f3427fad6209be3dc80365bdd5cd83455e62d17440b554ceb37f4d737f6cff43","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Translative-covering-densities-of-order-n-log-n-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L49"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are absolute constants $c>0$ and $n_0$ such that, for every integer\n$n\\ge n_0$, some centrally symmetric convex body $K_n\\subset\\mathbb R^n$\nsatisfies\n\\[\n \\theta_T(K_n)>c n\\log n.\n\\]"}
